Yes, you can block an issue from moving to another column in a JIRA board workflow if all items in a checklist are done marked as done. This can be achieved using the "Checklist" field and setting up a custom validation rule.

Here's how you can do it:

1. Create a custom field of type "Checklist" in your JIRA project. Let's call this field "Task List".
2. Add items to the Task List checklist that represent the tasks that need to be completed before the issue can be moved to the next column.
3. Go to your JIRA board settings and click on "Workflows" > "Edit" for the workflow you want to modify.
4. In the workflow editor, click on the "Transition" between the columns where you want to block the issue.
5. In the "Transition" properties, go to the "Validation" section and click on "Add Validation".
6. Choose "Custom Validation" and enter the following code in the "Validation Rule" field:
```
function validateTransition(issue) {
    var taskList = issue.getFieldValue("Task List");
    if (taskList && taskList.length > 0) {
        var allTasksDone = true;
        for (var i = 0; i < taskList.length; i++) {
            if (!issue.getFieldValue("task_" + i)) {
                allTasksDone = false;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (!allTasksDone) {
            return "Please complete all tasks in the Task List before transitioning.";
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```
This validation rule checks if the Task List field is not empty and if all tasks in the list are marked as done. If any task is not done, the issue will not be allowed to transition to the next column.

7. Save the workflow and test it by moving an issue to the transition between the columns. The issue should not be able to move unless all tasks in the Task List are marked as done.

Note that you can customize the validation rule to suit your specific needs. For example, you can add more conditions or messages to display when the validation fails.

